---
title: Plugin config
summary: Every option on the ogygia() Vite plugin — visible margins, presets, endpoint, rate limits, secret.
related:
  - reference/api
  - islands/server-islands
---

All tuning lives on the `ogygia()` Vite plugin. Every option is optional.

```ts
ogygia({
  visible: { margin: '120px' },
  presets: {
    demo: { wake: 'visible', margin: '200px' },
    frozenSwr: { wake: 'none', remount: { revalidate: 'load' } }
  }
})
```

## visible

Default `rootMargin` for `visible` islands and server islands, so they warm slightly before entering the viewport.

```ts
ogygia({ visible: { margin: '200px' } })
```

## presets

Named bundles of strategy + options, referenced from an import with `preset: 'name'`:

```svelte
<script>
  import Chart from './Chart.svelte' with { preset: 'demo' };
</script>
```

## stream

Turn on single-response server islands: `fill: 'load'` holes stream into the page's own response instead of a fetch each. See [Streaming & PPR](/docs/app/streaming-ppr).

```ts
ogygia({ stream: true })
```

## shell

Default shell-cache policy for opted-in routes — same API as lake `remount` (`'cache' | 'swr' | { revalidate, maxAge, onExpire }`). Per-route `export const shell` overrides it. See [Streaming & PPR](/docs/app/streaming-ppr).

```ts
ogygia({ shell: 'cache' })
```

## content

Turn on the markdown pipeline (mdsvex + Shiki + heading collection) for `.svx` / `.md` content collections. See [Markdown & Shiki](/docs/content/markdown).

```ts
ogygia({ content: { markdown: {} } })
```

## importKeys

Extra import-attribute keys to treat as ogygia directives, for interop with other tooling that reads import attributes.

## rateLimit

Guard the signed island endpoint against abuse — requests per window per client.

## sessionCookie

Name / options for the session cookie ogygia uses to scope signed capabilities.

## regionTtl

How long a signed region capability URL stays valid.

## OGYGIA_SECRET

The HMAC secret for signing `defer` capability URLs. Set it in the environment for stable signatures across a deployment; otherwise a per-build key is generated. Server islands and lake `remount: 'swr'` need the [server handle](/docs/start/install) installed to serve the endpoint.


